<title>GERMANY: BASF to build new plant in Antwerp.</title>
<headline>BASF to build new plant in Antwerp.</headline>
<dateline>LUDWIGSHAFEN, Germany 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and drugs group BASF AG said on Thursday that it plans to spend 27 million marks to build a plant to produce formaldehyde at its Antwerp complex.</p>
<p>The new plant will have an annual capacity of 40,000 tonnes and is expected to come on stream in 1998. Construction is scheduled to begin in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>Formaldehyde is used to make an important component for plastics production.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
